1
00:00:04,110 --> 00:00:12,770
A safety survey is a tool we use to proactively identify hazards and the corrective actions

2
00:00:12,770 --> 00:00:13,970
we need to take.

3
00:00:13,970 --> 00:00:18,850
Regular surveys are an important part of a company's occupational health and safety program.

4
00:00:18,850 --> 00:00:20,850
You're going to have a chance to practice.

5
00:00:20,850 --> 00:00:23,650
Your instructor will give you a survey checklist.

6
00:00:23,650 --> 00:00:27,850
But pay close attention because your instructor is sneaky and may have planted some hidden

7
00:00:27,850 --> 00:00:29,410
hazards.

8
00:00:29,410 --> 00:00:33,290
With this video, I want to share with you a few examples of the sort of things you'll

9
00:00:33,290 --> 00:00:34,290
be looking for.

10
00:00:34,790 --> 00:00:36,790
Let's head into the lab and begin our survey.

11
00:00:38,430 --> 00:00:40,830
Let's start with PPE.

12
00:00:40,830 --> 00:00:45,530
Lisa is wearing a lab coat, safety glasses, and gloves, which is always required for general

13
00:00:45,530 --> 00:00:46,810
lab work.

14
00:00:46,810 --> 00:00:48,530
She's also dressed appropriately.

15
00:00:48,530 --> 00:00:52,910
Closed-toed shoes, no jewelry, and her hair is tied back.

16
00:00:52,910 --> 00:00:57,350
You may need special PPE, depending on the work you're doing, like these heat-resistant

17
00:00:57,350 --> 00:00:59,910
gloves for opening the autoclave.

18
00:00:59,910 --> 00:01:01,510
That's PPE.

19
00:01:01,510 --> 00:01:03,910
Now let's look at some lab equipment.

20
00:01:04,170 --> 00:01:09,250
All equipment should be tested and certified to be sure it's in good working order.

21
00:01:09,250 --> 00:01:13,850
Fume hoods and biological safety cabinets look similar, but their functions are actually

22
00:01:13,850 --> 00:01:15,350
quite different.

23
00:01:15,350 --> 00:01:19,390
A fume hood is used to protect you when working with toxic chemicals.

24
00:01:19,390 --> 00:01:25,130
The airflow moves the vapors away from you, through a duct, and safely outside of a facility.

25
00:01:25,130 --> 00:01:29,190
This tag lets us know that the cabinet has been inspected and certified.

26
00:01:29,190 --> 00:01:34,550
A biological safety cabinet is used for working with infectious bacterial agents.

27
00:01:34,550 --> 00:01:38,950
The air flows through a HEPA filter to create a clean working environment, so it protects

28
00:01:38,950 --> 00:01:43,030
you, but also protects your work from contamination.

29
00:01:43,030 --> 00:01:47,590
This tag lets us know that the cabinet has been inspected and certified.

30
00:01:47,590 --> 00:01:49,870
Now let's look at some emergency gear.

31
00:01:49,870 --> 00:01:54,110
Know the location of your safety shower and eyewash station.

32
00:01:54,110 --> 00:01:58,330
Fire extinguisher and first aid kit.

33
00:01:58,330 --> 00:02:03,290
These areas must be kept clear of obstacles so you can get to them fast.

34
00:02:03,290 --> 00:02:07,090
Safety equipment also has to be regularly inspected and tagged.

35
00:02:07,090 --> 00:02:09,970
Be familiar with the emergency evacuation plan.

36
00:02:09,970 --> 00:02:15,560
An exit should be clear and marked.

37
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:17,040
Next is chemical safety.

38
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:20,640
All chemicals in the lab must be labeled and organized.

39
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:25,720
Labels provide important safety information like the chemical's properties, the manufacturer,

40
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:29,700
hazards, PPE, and storage requirements.

41
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:34,580
You can find even more details about the chemicals by looking at the safety data sheets.

42
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:40,480
Finally, let's survey some basic lab housekeeping requirements.

43
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:42,220
Always clean up after yourself.

44
00:02:42,220 --> 00:02:45,700
The lab should be organized and free of clutter.

45
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:49,580
Walkways should be clear of obstacles.

46
00:02:49,580 --> 00:02:54,480
Never bring food or drink in the lab, unless the food is being used for an experiment.

47
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:59,140
In that case, it should be labeled for lab use only.

48
00:02:59,140 --> 00:03:05,460
Dispose biological wastes in the container labeled with the appropriate biohazard symbol.

49
00:03:05,460 --> 00:03:08,860
Clean your equipment and workbench after each experiment.

50
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:15,740
And always place sharp objects like broken glassware in a sealable, puncture-proof container.

51
00:03:15,740 --> 00:03:19,940
These are just a handful of the items on your safety survey checklist.

52
00:03:19,940 --> 00:03:23,420
But hopefully this gives you a better idea of the type of things you'll be looking

53
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:25,460
for in your survey.

54
00:03:25,460 --> 00:03:27,980
Now head to the lab and get started.

55
00:03:27,980 --> 00:03:28,660
Thanks for watching.
